                    | With 12 million homes, the consumption of the residential and commercial sector in 2014 was: 11.4 × 10
                    sup 9
                    |  m
                    sup 3
                    |  of natural gas, 1.7 × 10
                    sup 6
                    |  Mg of LPG; 8 × 10
                    sup 6
                    |  Mg of firewood and 51 × 10
                    sup 6
                    |  MWh, leading to an average of 15.64 GJ/cap and 55.48 GJ/home (
                    a(href='#fig0010') Fig. 2
                    | ). Natural gas provides 52% of the total energy consumed by residential and commercial sectors for cooking and heating. While the Pampean Region has 20 million inhabitants consuming 54% of the total natural gas provision (460 m
                    sup 3
                    | /home per year), Patagonia, with 2.2 million inhabitants and the coldest climate in the country, consumed 24% of the natural gas provision (3,700 m
                    sup 3
                    | /home per year), other Regions consumed the remaining 22% (
                    a(href='#fig0015') Fig. 3
                    | ). Emissions to the atmosphere from the use of electricity in homes and offices are estimated as emissions from thermal power plants (next section).
